 We are looking for an Executive Director (ED) to be a Global Advisor for Non\-Bank Financial Institution (NBFI) and Corporate clients. This role is responsible for building a regional network across existing and new client opportunities and generating the strategies, content, articles, speaking engagements and other tools to help drive sales success. The role requires strong market expertise to work with companies in need of a global banking partner’s scale and capability depth.
   

  

 The role will act as the ‘go\-to’ for all opportunities in the APAC region in 1\-2 sectors and be the conduit for information, themes, solutions, case studies etc to flow in and out across the sales/banking organization.
   

  

 The role will involve work at a client level, an industry thematic level and with general Treasury practice matters. In addition, the role is market facing and should drive key industry and proprietary events which help position J.P. Morgan Payments as the market leader.
   

  

 This person will support in the execution of the growth strategy working closely with Product, Sales, Bankers, and Business Development to identify priority clients and sub\- segments, defining sales strategies, participating in proactive client engagement, collaborating with a wide array of internal stakeholders and functional partners, and developing solutions for strategic and complex deals. Responsibilities include creating a roadmap to capture addressable wallet, assessing the future of the industry and positioning the business development and sales teams for success.
   

  

 The role reports to the Global Head of Advisory for South Asia. The role is a single point of accountability for driving sales success assisted by the objective, trusted advisor position of the Global Advisory team.
   

  

**Job Responsibilities**
* Work independently and in partnership with the Global Industry teams to develop and deliver treasury best practices, industry trends, benchmarking, compelling market analysis and banking solutions aligned with key priorities and needs of clients
