li-4368124208,Sales Development Representative,Teleport,"Chatuchak, Bangkok City, Thailand",01/02/2026,fulltime,entry level,Other,"**About Teleport**
 Teleport is Southeast Asia's leading integrated logistics provider, on a mission to make logistics faster, more affordable, and more reliable. We are building the infrastructure to make next\-day delivery accessible across the region \- moving things better than anyone else.
   

  

**Role Overview**
 We are looking for a driven
 **Sales Development Representative (SDR)** 
 to accelerate customer acquisition by engaging and qualifying inbound leads, and converting them into high\-quality opportunities.
   

  

 You will be the
 **first point of contact** 
 for prospective customers \- shaping their first impression of Teleport while ensuring that well\-qualified opportunities move efficiently through the sales funnel. This role is a key driver of sales productivity and plays an important part in building foundational sales knowledge (scripts, FAQs, call insights) that supports future automation and scaling.
   

  

**Key Responsibilities**
* Lead Engagement \& Qualification
* Proactively engage inbound leads from paid campaigns via calls and messaging
* Qualify prospects based on defined criteria (use case, shipment volume, urgency, operational fit)
* Understand customer needs and position relevant Teleport solutions
* Schedule qualified meetings for the BD team with clear context and notes
* CRM \& Process Excellence
* Maintain accurate and up\-to\-date deal records in HubSpot
* Log call outcomes, customer requirements, objections, and next steps
* Manage and prioritize 200\+ active leads efficiently
* Ensure structured and complete handover to the BD team
* Customer Activation
* Reach out to new platform sign\-ups to guide them toward placing their first order
* Address basic pricing, operational, and onboarding questions
* Identify and reduce early\-stage customer friction
* Escalate complex issues to the relevant teams when needed
* Insights \& Continuous Improvement
* Capture recurring customer questions, objections, and pain points
* Share insights with Product, Commercial, and Operations teams
* Contribute to the development of call scripts, FAQs, and sales playbooks
* Support improvements that increase lead\-to\-meeting and activation rates


**Requirements**
****Qualifications****
**Experience**
* 1 \- 3 years of experience in sales, telesales, customer engagement, or lead qualification
* Experience handling high volumes of leads or customer interactions
* Exposure to logistics, e\-commerce, SaaS, or marketplace businesses is a plus
* Experience using a CRM system (HubSpot preferred)


**Skills**
* Strong phone presence and written communication skills
* Good at understanding customer needs quickly
* Organized with strong follow\-up discipline
* Comfortable managing multiple leads and conversations simultaneously
* Able to follow processes while adapting to different customer situations
* Basic data awareness \- able to notice common patterns in conversations",IT Services and IT Consulting,Thailand,Full-time,Entry,0,1,0,1,0,0,0,1,1
li-4366002076,"Sales Development Representative (SDR) – Bangkok, Thailand",TableCheck,"Bang Rak, Bangkok City, Thailand",27/01/2026,fulltime,entry level,Sales and Business Development,"**About TableCheck**
 TableCheck is a global platform built to help restaurants own their guest experience.
   

  

 We help merchants reduce their reliance on paid booking channels by directly converting first\-time diners into repeat guests⁠—and repeat guests into loyal fans.
   

  

 Used by over 13,000\+ restaurants in 35 countries–including over 300\+ Michelin\-starred restaurants and top hospitality brands such as Hyatt, Hilton and IHG. TableCheck has set new standards for restaurant management tools in Japan and is steadily growing to take on the challenge to become the world’s leader in restaurant management.
   

  

**About The Role**
 The
 **Sales Development Representative (SDR)** 
 will create new business sales opportunities for TableCheck. SDRs will research restaurants, hotels, and hospitality operators in the Asean region. Then, the SDR will create an outreach plan and determine how these operators can benefit from using the TableCheck platform. SDRs will identify, engage, and qualify prospects that fit within our target customer profile. You will play an important role in the sales process by promoting the power of our one of a kind guest experience and retention platform through introductory and discovery calls. Our most successful SDRs are curious, autonomous, and goal\-focused. You are someone that connects and builds positive relationships with people from all walks of life.
   

  

**Duties \& Responsibilities**
**・Prospecting:** 
 Identify and research potential customers and decision makers using various tools; build targeted lists for outreach.
   

  

**・Outreach \& research** 
 : Execute multichannel outbound campaigns (cold calls, emails, social outreach); test and adopt tools/techniques to improve contact discovery and outreach effectiveness.
   

  

**・Engagement** 
