 The Regional Project Development Manager within the Siemens Energy Compression business is a key technical sales function within the organization, responsible for driving sales \& solution development. You will be responsible for achieving the segment sales targets and growth objective along with the high performing regional sales team while identifying new business opportunities and developing technical solutions with key customers.
   

  

 This role will require close partnerships with our customer relationship team and shall be the conduit into the bid management, engineering, and global product centres. You will create \& develop regional service \& aftermarket compression leads across all of Asia Pacific develop technical solutions, cost modelling, \& valued proposals while also working in close collaboration with our global operational team located in the Americas, Europe, Africa, Middle East, \& Asia Pacific to deliver order entry growth \& operational excellence.
   

  

 This role will report directly to the Global Head of Sales \& Bid Management for the Siemens Energy segment business.
   

  

 We are looking for a highly experienced, self\-motivated, dynamic, customer\-focused leader that looks at shaping the Compression business for future generations!
   

  

**How You’ll Make An Impact**
* Lead the overall sales development process for complex projects to standard aftermarket services related to centrifugal compressors, reciprocating compressors, geared compressors, and gas engines
* Responsible for Opportunity discovery \& qualification; strategy setting \& development
* Identifying \& influencing key decision makers and successfully navigating complex internal \& external selling environments.
* Drive service business growth across all core markets and portfolio including Modernization \& Upgrades, Repair, Field Service, Parts, Controls, Digitalization, \& Service Programs.
* Exercise solid business acumen to develop and articulate a unique winning value proposition while maintaining company growth and profit guidelines.
* Build and maintain strong relationships with key customers \& partners, understanding their needs to develop tailored solutions, and ensure customer satisfaction by delivering exceptional service and support.
* Work closely with senior leadership to develop and implement a comprehensive sales strategy to ensure successful implementation across the regional business.
* Responsible for Forecasting all segment service business across the European regional territory– Salesforce funnel, and accuracy / quality of forecasts.
* Leading handover process to the commercial and executing teams for every new project. Responsibilities include final Purchase Order review and capture; and leading/participating in all internal and external kick\-off meetings.
* Participate and potentially lead SE business growth initiatives as needed.
* Meet sales targets and earnings objectives while representing the customer requirements.
* Monitor market \& industry trend activity.
* Perform regular financial analysis \& report out on key performance indicators.


**What You Bring**
* Bachelor’s in Engineering or related field is preferred. Must have at least 7 years of experience in technical sales, marketing, business development, or strategy in oil \& gas, power generation, or industrial services sectors, proving success in diverse markets.
* Strong knowledge \& diverse background in various compressors or industrial rotating equipment suppliers. Previous experience working for a major rotating equipment supplier is preferred.
